strong class='sig'>+0.81\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.51 to +1.11) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.58\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.21 to +0.94). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 4 of 12 months. Highs rose in none.","t_rain":"Jackson has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Jackson's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.69 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.24 to +1.14), about +8.9 inches since 1896. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 57.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 1979 (92.75 in); the driest, 1952 (31.66 in). Jackson almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.9 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}